Before editing Teamflow code:

1. Read `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` for the layout, auth model and conventions.
2. Read the doc for the area you are changing (`docs/AUTH.md`, `docs/ATTACHMENTS.md`, `docs/MCP.md`, `docs/CLI.md`, `docs/discord-bot.md`, `docs/SELF-HOSTING.md`). Route changes: run `pnpm docs:api` to regenerate `docs/API.md`.
3. Maintainers may keep local, gitignored planning notes in `docs/`; read them if your checkout has them, but never link to them from committed files.

After completing work, update the public doc for that area. Run `pnpm test`, `pnpm lint` and `pnpm typecheck` with Node 20.

Deployment: Setup A (Windows native) and Setup B (Proxmox LXC). Docker is an optional extra, not a primary path. SQLite only; Postgres is deferred.
